# LeetCode 643 — Maximum Average Subarray I

Pattern: Fixed-Size Sliding Window

Problem: Integer array `nums` aur integer `k` diya hai. Size exactly `k` wale contiguous subarray ka maximum average find karna hai.

Example:

```
Input:  nums = [1, 12, -5, -6, 50, 3], k = 4
Output: 12.75
```

Kyunki maximum-sum subarray hai `[12, -5, -6, 50]`.

\\[ \text{Average}=\frac{12+(-5)+(-6)+50}{4} =\frac{51}{4}=12.75 \\]

## Approach 1: Brute Force

Har possible size-`k` subarray ka sum calculate karo, phir maximum average find karo.

```
class Solution {
    public double findMaxAverage(int[] nums, int k) {
        double maxAverage = Double.NEGATIVE_INFINITY;

        // Har possible starting index check karo
        for (int i = 0; i <= nums.length - k; i++) {
            int sum = 0;

            // Size k ke subarray ka sum nikalo
            for (int j = i; j < i + k; j++) {
                sum += nums[j];
            }

            double average = (double) sum / k;
            maxAverage = Math.max(maxAverage, average);
        }

        return maxAverage;
    }
}
```

- Time: \\(O(nk)\\)
- Extra Space: \\(O(1)\\)

## Approach 2: Better — Prefix Sum

Idea: Prefix sum array banao, jisse kisi bhi subarray ka sum \\(O(1)\\) time mein nikal sakein.

```
class Solution {
    public double findMaxAverage(int[] nums, int k) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int[] prefix = new int[n + 1];

        // Prefix sum calculate karo
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            prefix[i + 1] = prefix[i] + nums[i];
        }

        int maxSum = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

        // Har size-k window ka sum nikalo
        for (int i = 0; i <= n - k; i++) {
            int sum = prefix[i + k] - prefix[i];
            maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, sum);
        }

        return (double) maxSum / k;
    }
}
```

- Time: \\(O(n)\\)
- Extra Space: \\(O(n)\\)

## Approach 3: Optimal — Fixed-Size Sliding Window

Recommended

Idea: Pehle `k` elements ka sum nikalo. Phir window ko ek position right slide karo:

- Purana leftmost element subtract karo.
- Naya rightmost element add karo.
- Maximum window sum update karo.

Is tarah har window ke liye poora sum dobara calculate nahi karna padta.

```
class Solution {
    public double findMaxAverage(int[] nums, int k) {
        int sum = 0;

        // First window ka sum
        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {
            sum += nums[i];
        }

        int maxSum = sum;

        // Window ko ek-ek position right slide karo
        for (int i = k; i < nums.length; i++) {
            sum = sum - nums[i - k] + nums[i];

            // Maximum sum update karo
            maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, sum);
        }

        // Average calculate karo
        return (double) maxSum / k;
    }
}
```

### Dry Run

Input: `nums = [1, 12, -5, -6, 50, 3]`, `k = 4`

| Window             | Sum | Maximum Sum |
| ------------------ | --- | ----------- |
| `[1, 12, -5, -6]`  | 2   | 2           |
| `[12, -5, -6, 50]` | 51  | 51          |
| `[-5, -6, 50, 3]`  | 42  | 51          |

Final answer: \\(51/4 = 12.75\\)

